myelin 1
id      three
about   three.js r186 on the WebGPU + TSL path (WebGPURenderer, RenderPipeline, node materials): bans APIs models learned from older releases and WebGL-only patterns that do not run under WebGPURenderer
fires   three.js | threejs | three/webgpu | three/tsl | three/addons | WebGPURenderer | TSL | RenderPipeline | EffectComposer | WebGLRenderer | GLTFLoader | OrbitControls
comments skip
status  Researched 2026-10-26 against r186 (npm three@0.186.1): migration guide, r170-r186 release notes, threejs.org/docs + manual + docs/llms.txt, r186 source. Targets the WebGPU path: WebGLRenderer, EffectComposer, ShaderMaterial and onBeforeCompile still exist for WebGL apps but are banned here; do not load this ledger for an intentionally WebGLRenderer-only project. Regex-level checks. Snippets not executed on a GPU.

= version     three.js r186 (npm three@0.186.1, released 2026-09-08; r187 is in development and NOT released, so do not use its changes yet)
= verified    2026-10-26
= imports     import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu'; TSL from 'three/tsl'; addons from 'three/addons/...'; post effects from 'three/addons/tsl/display/<Name>Node.js'
= importmap   "three": ".../build/three.webgpu.js", "three/webgpu": same, "three/tsl": ".../build/three.tsl.js", "three/addons/": ".../examples/jsm/"
= renderer    new THREE.WebGPURenderer(); renderer.setAnimationLoop(fn) auto-initialises; call await renderer.init() before any render/compute outside the loop
= post        new THREE.RenderPipeline(renderer); pass(scene, camera); renderPipeline.outputNode = ...; renderPipeline.render() replaces renderer.render()
= effects     bloom BloomNode.js | traa TRAANode.js | ao GTAONode.js | ssao SSAONode.js | ssr SSRNode.js | dof DepthOfFieldNode.js | fxaa FXAANode.js | smaa SMAANode.js | film FilmNode.js | gaussianBlur GaussianBlurNode.js
= time        THREE.Timer (core since r179): timer.connect(document); timer.update() each frame; getDelta() / getElapsed(). TSL: time, deltaTime
= color       renderer.outputColorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace (default); texture.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace for color maps

! B1 /\bnew\s+(THREE\.)?PostProcessing\s*\(|\{[^}]*\bPostProcessing\b[^}]*\}\s*from/   PostProcessing was renamed RenderPipeline in r183 (old name is a deprecated alias). Use new THREE.RenderPipeline(renderer) and renderPipeline.render(). -> $bloom
! B2 /\b(EffectComposer|ShaderPass|UnrealBloomPass)\b|(addons|jsm)\/postprocessing\//   EffectComposer and its passes only work with WebGLRenderer. On WebGPURenderer use RenderPipeline + pass() + effect nodes from 'three/addons/tsl/display/' (bloom, traa, ao, ssr, fxaa, smaa, dof...). -> $bloom
! B3 /\b(Raw)?ShaderMaterial\b/   ShaderMaterial/RawShaderMaterial (raw GLSL) only work with WebGLRenderer. Write the shader in TSL on a *NodeMaterial (colorNode, positionNode, normalNode, fragmentNode...). -> $tslmat
! B4 /\bonBeforeCompile\b/   onBeforeCompile shader patching is not supported by WebGPURenderer. Override node inputs with TSL instead (material.colorNode = texture(map).mul(detail)). -> $tslmat
! B5 /\bnew\s+(THREE\.)?Clock\s*\(/   THREE.Clock is deprecated since r183. Use THREE.Timer: timer.connect(document); call timer.update() once per frame, then timer.getDelta() / timer.getElapsed(). -> $boot
! B6 /\bPCFSoftShadowMap\b/   PCFSoftShadowMap was removed in r186 (both renderers warn and fall back). Use THREE.PCFShadowMap, which is soft now (tune light.shadow.radius). -> $shadows
! B7 /\b(outputEncoding|sRGBEncoding|LinearEncoding|GammaEncoding|legacyMode)\b|\.encoding\s*=/   The encoding API was replaced in r152 and removed in r162: renderer.outputColorSpace / texture.colorSpace with THREE.SRGBColorSpace / THREE.LinearSRGBColorSpace; ColorManagement is enabled by default. -> $color
! B8 /\b(useLegacyLights|physicallyCorrectLights)\b/   Legacy lighting switches were removed (physicallyCorrectLights in r160, useLegacyLights in r165). Physically based light units are the only mode; delete the line and retune intensities.
! B9 /\b(Box|Sphere|Plane|Cylinder|Cone|Circle|Ring|Torus|TorusKnot|Tetrahedron|Octahedron|Icosahedron|Dodecahedron|Polyhedron|Lathe|Extrude|Shape|Tube|Edges|Wireframe|Capsule|Text|Parametric|RoundedBox|Teapot)BufferGeometry\b/   The *BufferGeometry aliases are gone (deprecated r145, removed r154). Use BoxGeometry, SphereGeometry, PlaneGeometry, ... (they already return BufferGeometry). -> $tslmat
! B10 /\bTHREE\.(Geometry|Face3|Math)\b|\bnew\s+(Geometry|Face3)\s*\(/   Geometry and Face3 were removed (r125); THREE.Math is THREE.MathUtils. Build a BufferGeometry with setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(array, 3)).
! B11 /examples\/js\/|\/build\/three\.js\b|\bthree(\.module|\.webgpu|\.core|\.tsl)?\.min\.js\b/   Removed builds: examples/js (r148), build/three.js and three.min.js (r161), and the shipped *.min.js files (r186; unpkg/cdnjs links 404). Use ES modules with an import map. -> $importmap
! B12 /['"]three\/examples\/jsm\//   Import addons through the documented 'three/addons/' path (maps to examples/jsm/), e.g. 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js'. -> $boot
! B13 /['"]three\/nodes['"\/]|\bjsm\/nodes\/|renderers\/webgpu\/WebGPURenderer(\.js)?['"]/   Pre-r171 WebGPU import paths no longer exist. Import WebGPURenderer and node materials from 'three/webgpu' and TSL from 'three/tsl'. -> $boot
! B14 /\bnew\s+(THREE\.)?WebGLRenderer\s*\(/   This ledger targets the WebGPU path: use new THREE.WebGPURenderer() from 'three/webgpu' (falls back to WebGL 2 automatically). WebGLRenderer is not removed; if the project must stay WebGL-only, this ledger does not apply. -> $boot
! B15 /\b(tslFn|timerLocal|timerGlobal|timerDelta|directionToColor|colorToDirection)\b/   Renamed TSL functions: tslFn -> Fn (r168); timerLocal/timerGlobal/timerDelta -> time / deltaTime (r170); directionToColor -> packNormalToRGB, colorToDirection -> unpackRGBToNormal (r185). -> $tslmat
! B16 /\.(renderAsync|clearAsync|hasFeatureAsync|initTextureAsync)\s*\(/   The *Async renderer methods are deprecated since r181. Initialise once (setAnimationLoop or await renderer.init()), then call render(), clear(), hasFeature(), initTexture(). -> $boot
! B17 /\bcolorBufferType\b|\bgetColorBufferType\s*\(/   WebGPURenderer's colorBufferType option was renamed outputBufferType in r182 (getOutputBufferType()). -> $boot
! B18 /\bRGBELoader\b/   RGBELoader was renamed HDRLoader in r180 (old name is a deprecated alias): import { HDRLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/HDRLoader.js'. -> $env
! B19 /\bWebGLCubeRenderTarget\b/   WebGLCubeRenderTarget cannot be used with WebGPURenderer since r183. Use THREE.CubeRenderTarget from 'three/webgpu'.
! B20 /\bTRAAPassNode\b|\btraaPass\s*\(/   TRAAPassNode/traaPass() became TRAANode/traa(color, depth, velocity, camera) in r179; the scene pass needs an MRT with velocity. -> $traa
! B21 /\b(distanceExponent|distanceFallOff)\b/   GTAONode distanceExponent/distanceFallOff are deprecated in r186 and have no effect (new distance model). Tune radius, scale and thickness instead; use only the AO .r channel. -> $ao

~ P1 Use *NodeMaterial classes (MeshStandardNodeMaterial, MeshPhysicalNodeMaterial, ...) whenever you assign node slots; plain MeshStandardMaterial still renders under WebGPURenderer but has no colorNode/positionNode.
~ P2 With a RenderPipeline, render through renderPipeline.render() in the loop, not renderer.render(scene, camera). Set renderPipeline.needsUpdate = true after swapping outputNode.
~ P3 Tone mapping and output color space are applied once at the end of RenderPipeline. For FXAA or LUT grading set renderPipeline.outputColorTransform = false and insert renderOutput() yourself.
~ P4 SSR: add reflections additively (scenePassColor.add(ssrPass.rgb)), not blendColor (changed r183). GTAO: use only the .r channel and feed it via scenePass.contextNode = builtinAOContext(aoPass.getTextureNode().sample(screenUV).r). -> $ao
~ P5 Shadows on WebGPURenderer improved in r183: start with no shadow.bias (or a much smaller one) before adding any.
~ P6 For skinned/morphed meshes, read untransformed vertices with positionGeometry in positionNode (r185); positionLocal no longer re-applies skinning there.
~ P7 TransformControls: add controls.getHelper() to the scene, not the controls object (r169).
~ P8 Do not assume r187 changes (CubeUVReflectionMapping removal, iridescenceThicknessMinimum/Maximum, struct storage .element(0)) until r187 is released.

